1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,880
As a daughter of an immigrant, it is imperative that black people from other places understand

2
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:10,680
the disparate difference that they exist from black people in the United States.

3
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:13,620
It is not the same, period.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,680
And ultimately, the best effort that we can do as a diaspora is to lead in understanding,

5
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:21,860
not in judgment.

6
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:27,780
So when I am talking to somebody from Sudan, from the Congo, from Angola, I am listening

7
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:30,140
to understand their experience, not to undermine it.

8
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:35,440
And I refuse to allow anybody from Grenada, from Angola, from any other place to come

9
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:37,460
and try to undermine the experience of black Americans.

